# Accepted gitleaks findings, with the reason each is accepted.
#
# EMPTY, AND THAT IS EARNED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. This repository begins at a
# single seed commit (ADR-0114), so the three fingerprints this file used to
# carry pinned commits it does not have -- and one named a file it does not
# hold. Removing them was correct. Assuming nothing would then be found was NOT:
# the first CI run on the public repository flagged Plex's GPG public key
# fingerprint, still live in the working file, and the note those entries
# carried ("the values have been redacted from the working files") turned out to
# be true of one value and not the other.
#
# So the second one is redacted now too, in the file, beside a sentence saying
# what was removed and why. That is the durable fix: a fingerprint is
# `commit:file:rule:line`, so it dies again on the next commit that touches the
# file, while a redaction holds.
#
# Do not add to this file to make a check pass. If a finding is genuinely ours,
# rotate the credential -- do not record it here. If it is a third-party public
# value quoted as research evidence, redact it from the working file and say so
# beside the quotation.
